{
  "title": "51: al-Zaareyaat الذاريات",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nوَالذّٰرِيٰتِ ذَرْوًا ۙ‏(1)\nWAALZZAAREETE ZARWAN.\nBy the scatterers that Scatter,\nفَالْحٰمِلٰتِ وِقْرًا ۙ‏(2)\nFAL HAAMELAATE WEQRAN.\nThen those which bear their load,\nفَالْجٰرِيٰتِ يُسْرًا ۙ‏(3)\nFAL JAAREETE YUSRAN.\nThen by those which speed lightly along,\nفَالْمُقَسِّمٰتِ اَمْرًا ۙ‏(4)\nFAL MUQASSEMAATE AMRAN.\nThen by those distribute the affair,\nاِنَّمَا تُوْعَدُوْنَ لَصَادِقٌ ۙ‏(5)\nINNAMAA TOO-A’DOON LASAADEQUN.\nVerily what ye are threatened with, is certainly true,\nوَّاِنَّ الدِّيْنَ لوَاقِعٌ ؕ‏(6)\nWWAANNA DEENA LWAAQEA’UN.\nAnd verily the Judgment shall surely come to pass.\nوَالسَّمَآءِ ذَاتِ الْحُبُكِ ۙ‏(7)\nWAS SAMAAA-E ZAATIL AL-HUBUKE.\nAnd by the heaven with its starry highways,\nاِنَّكُمْ لَفِىْ قَوْلٍ مُّخْتَلِفٍ ۙ‏(8)\nINNAKUM LAFEE QAWLIN MMUKHTALEFIN.\nVerily ye are in discordance in what ye say,\nيُّؤْفَكُ عَنْهُ مَنْ اُفِكَ ؕ‏(9)\nYYUFAKU A’NHO MAN AUFEKA.\nHe will be turned away from it who is to be turned away.\nقُتِلَ الْخَرّٰصُوْنَۙ‏(10)\nQOTELAL AL-KHARRAASOONA.\nAccursed be the conjecturers,\nالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ فِىْ غَمْرَةٍ سَاهُوْنَۙ‏(11)\nLAZEENA HUM FEE GHAMRATIN SAAHOONAL.\nWho in the abyss (of ignorance) are wandering (bewildered),\nيَسْئَلُوْنَ اَيَّانَ يَوْمُ الدِّيْنِؕ‏(12)\nYAS-ALOONAN AYYAANA YAWMUD DEEN.\nAsk they: “When is the Day of Judgment?\nيَوْمَ هُمْ عَلَى النَّارِ يُفْتَنُوْنَ‏(13)\nYAWMA HUM A’LAL NAAR LAA YUFTANOON.\nOn that day shall they be tried at the fire.\nذُوْقُوْا فِتْنَتَكُمْؕ هٰذَا الَّذِىْ كُنْتُمْ بِهٖ تَسْتَعْجِلُوْنَ‏(14)\nZOOQOO FETNATAKUM HAAZAA LAZEE KUNTUM BEHI TAS-TA’JELOONA.\n(It will be said) “Taste ye (now) your trial (on the fire); This is what ye did seek to hasten on!\nاِنَّ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ فِىْ جَنّٰتٍ وَّعُيُوْنٍۙ‏(15)\nINNAL MA-A’L MUTTAQEEN FEE JANNAATIN WA O’OYOONINW.\nVerily the pious ones shall be in gardens and (among the) springs,\nاٰخِذِيْنَ مَاۤ اٰتٰٮهُمْ رَبُّهُمْ‌ؕ اِنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا قَبْلَ ذٰلِكَ مُحْسِنِيْنَؕ‏(16)\nAAAKHEZEENA MAA AAATAAHUM RABBUHUM INNAHUM KAANOO QABLA ZAALEKA MUHSENEENA.\nReceiving (the enjoyment) what giveth them their Lord; Verily, they were ere that the doers of good.\nكَانُوْا قَلِيْلًا مِّنَ الَّيْلِ مَا يَهْجَعُوْنَ‏(17)\nKAANOO QALEELAA MENAL LAYLE MAA YAHJAU’OONA.\nLittle of the night was it that they used to sleep.\nوَبِالْاَسْحَارِ هُمْ يَسْتَغْفِرُوْنَ‏(18)\nWABEALAASHAARE HUM YASTAGHFEROONA.\nAnd in the (hours) ere the dawn they prayed for forgiveness.\nوَفِىْۤ اَمْوَالِهِمْ حَقٌّ لِّلسَّآئِلِ وَالْمَحْرُوْمِ‏(19)\nWA FEE AAMWAALEHEM HAQQUWN LLELSSAAELE WAL MAHROOME.\nAnd in their property was a share due to the beggar and the destitute.\nوَفِى الْاَرْضِ اٰيٰتٌ لِّلْمُوْقِنِيْنَۙ‏(20)\nWA ARZE AAYAATUM LLELMOOQENEENA.\nAnd in the earth are signs for those who are sure in faith,\nوَفِىْۤ اَنْفُسِكُمْ‌ؕ اَفَلَا تُبْصِرُوْنَ‏(21)\nWA FEE ANFOSEKUM AFALAA TUBSEROON.\nAnd (also) in your own selves; will ye not then see?\nوَفِى السَّمَآءِ رِزْقُكُمْ وَمَا تُوْعَدُوْنَ‏(22)\nWA SAMAAA-E REZQUKUM WA MAA TOO-A’DOON.\nAnd in the heaven is your sustenance and what ye are promised with.\nفَوَرَبِّ السَّمَآءِ وَالْاَرْضِ اِنَّهٗ لَحَقٌّ مِّثْلَ مَاۤ اَنَّكُمْ تَنْطِقُوْنَ‏(23)\nFAWARABBE SAMAAA-E WAL ARZE INNAHU LAHAQQUN MISLA MAA ANNAKUM TANTEQOONA.\nAnd by the Lord of the heavens and the earth! verily It (the Qur'an) is certainly the truth, just as ye speak,\nهَلْ اَتٰٮكَ حَدِيْثُ ضَيْفِ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ الْمُكْرَمِيْنَ‌ۘ‏(24)\nHAL ATAAKA HADEESUL ZAYFE IBRAAHEEMA MUKRAMEEN.\nHas there come unto thee [O Muhammad] the story of Abraham’s honoured guests?\nاِذْ دَخَلُوْا عَلَيْهِ فَقَالُوْا سَلٰمًا‌ؕ قَالَ سَلٰمٌ ۚ قَوْمٌ مُّنْكَرُوْنَ‌‏(25)\nIZ DAKHALOO A’LAYHE FA-QAALOO SALAAMAN QAALA SALAAMUN QAWMUN MMUNKAROONA.\nWhen entered they upon him said they: ‘Peace!’. ‘Peace! Said he [and deemed] A strange people [these are]\nفَرَاغَ اِلٰٓى اَهْلِهٖ فَجَآءَ بِعِجْلٍ سَمِيْنٍۙ‏(26)\nFARAAGHA ELAA AHLEHI FA JAAA-A BEE’EJLIN SAMEENIN.\nThen turned he aside unto his family, and brought a fat (roasted) calf\nفَقَرَّبَهٗۤ اِلَيْهِمْ قَالَ اَلَا تَاْكُلُوْنَ‏(27)\nFAQARRABAH ELAYHIM QAALA ALAA TAAKULOONA.\nAnd set it near them. He said: ‘What! Eat ye not?\nفَاَوْجَسَ مِنْهُمْ خِيْفَةً‌ؕ قَالُوْا لَا تَخَفْ‌ ؕ وَبَشَّرُوْهُ بِغُلٰمٍ عَلِيْمٍ‏(28)\nFAAWJASA MINHUM KHEEFATAN QAALOO LAA TAKHAF WABASSHAROOHU BEGHULAAMIN A’LEEM.\nAnd he conceived of them a fear; Said they: “Fear thou not!” and gave they the glad tidings unto him of a son blessed with knowledge\nفَاَقْبَلَتِ امْرَاَتُهٗ فِىْ صَرَّةٍ فَصَكَّتْ وَجْهَهَا وَقَالَتْ عَجُوْزٌ عَقِيْمٌ‏(29)\nFAAQBALATE AMRAATUH FEE SARRATIN FASAKKAT WAJHAHAA WA QAALAT A’AJOOZUN A’AQEEMUN.\nThen came forward his wife in grief, she smote her face and said she (what! I) an old barren woman?\nقَالُوْا كَذٰلِكِ ۙ قَالَ رَبُّكِ‌ؕ اِنَّهٗ هُوَ الْحَكِيْمُ الْعَلِيْمُ‏(30)\nQAALOO KAZAALEKE QAALA RABBUKE INNAHU HOWA HAKEEM A’LEEM.\nSaid they: “Thus sayeth thy Lord: ‘Verily He is the All-Wise, the All-Knowing\nقَالَ فَمَا خَطْبُكُمْ اَيُّهَا الْمُرْسَلُوْنَ‏(31)\nQAALA FAMAA KHATBUKUM AYYOHAL MURSALOON.\nHe said “What then is your errand, O’ ye Messengers?\nقَالُوْۤا اِنَّاۤ اُرْسِلْنَاۤ اِلٰى قَوْمٍ مُّجْرِمِيْنَۙ‏(32)\nQAALOO INNAA AURSELNAA ELAA QAWMIN MMUJREMEENA.\nSaid they: ‘We are sent unto a criminal people\nلِنُرْسِلَ عَلَيْهِمْ حِجَارَةً مِّنْ طِيْنٍۙ‏(33)\nLENURSELA A’LAYHIM HEJAARATAN MIN TEENIN.\nThat We may send down upon them stones of clay\nمُّسَوَّمَةً عِنْدَ رَبِّكَ لِلْمُسْرِفِيْنَ‏(34)\nMMUSAWMATAN I’NDAL RABBEKA LIL-MUSREFEENA.\nMarked out from unto thy Lord for the guilty ones of excesses\nفَاَخْرَجْنَا مَنْ كَانَ فِيْهَا مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(35)\nFA AKH-RAJNAA MAN KAANA FEEHAA MENAL MOAMENEEN.\nAnd We brought forth (those) who were there in (the town) of the believers\nفَمَا وَجَدْنَا فِيْهَا غَيْرَ بَيْتٍ مِّنَ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(36)\nFAMAA WAJADNAA FEEHAA GHAYRA BAYTIYN MENAL AKOONA MENAL MUSLEMEEN.\nBut We found not there in (the town) save one house of the Muslims\nوَتَرَكْنَا فِيْهَاۤ اٰيَةً لِّلَّذِيْنَ يَخَافُوْنَ الْعَذَابَ الْاَلِيْمَؕ‏(37)\nWATARAKNAA FEEHAA AAYATAL LIL-LAZEENA YAKHAAFOONA A’ZAABA AL-AALEEMA.\nAnd left We therein a sign for those who dread the painful chastisement\nوَفِىْ مُوْسٰۤی اِذْ اَرْسَلْنٰهُ اِلٰى فِرْعَوْنَ بِسُلْطٰنٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(38)\nWA FEE MOOSAA IZ AARSALNAAHU ELAA FIR-A’WNA BESULTAANIM MOBEEN.\nAnd in Moses, when We sent him unto Pharaoh with manifest authority\nفَتَوَلّٰى بِرُكْنِهٖ وَقَالَ سٰحِرٌ اَوْ مَجْنُوْنٌ‏(39)\nFA TAWALLAA BERUKNEH WA QAALA SAAHERUN AW MAJNOONUN.\nBut (Pharaoh) turned away with his forces and said (pointing to Moses): ‘(This is) a sorcerer or a madman\nفَاَخَذْنٰهُ وَجُنُوْدَهٗ فَنَبَذْنٰهُمْ فِى الْيَمِّ وَهُوَ مُلِيْمٌؕ‏(40)\nFA-AKHAZNAAHO WA JONOODOHU FANABAZNAAHUM FIL WA WA HOWA MULEEMUN.\nSo, We seized him and his hosts and We cast them into the sea, for he was reprobate\nوَفِىْ عَادٍ اِذْ اَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِمُ الرِّيْحَ الْعَقِيْمَ‌ۚ‏(41)\nWA FEE A’ADIN IZ ARSALNAA A’LAYHEMUL AR-REEHA AL-A’AQEEMA.\nAnd in ‘Ad: when sent We upon them the desolating (blast of violent’) wind\nمَا تَذَرُ مِنْ شَىْءٍ اَتَتْ عَلَيْهِ اِلَّا جَعَلَتْهُ كَالرَّمِيْمِؕ‏(42)\nMAA TAZARU MIN SHAY-IN AATAT A’LAYHE ILLAA JAA’ALATHU KAALRRAMEEME.\nIt left not aught upon which it came, but turned it like (rotten) dust\nوَفِىْ ثَمُوْدَ اِذْ قِيْلَ لَهُمْ تَمَتَّعُوْا حَتّٰى حِيْنٍ‏(43)\nWA FEE ELAA IZ QEELA LAHUM TAMATTAU’OOA HATTAA HEEN.\nAnd in Thamood: when it was said unto them; “Avail ye your- selves for a while\nفَعَتَوْا عَنْ اَمْرِ رَبِّهِمْ فَاَخَذَتْهُمُ الصّٰعِقَةُ وَ هُمْ يَنْظُرُوْنَ‏(44)\nFAA’ATAWA A’N AMRE RABBEHIM FA-AKHAZATHOMUR SAA-E’QATO WA HUM YANZOROONA.\nBut rebelled they against the command of their Lord, so seized them the rumbling, while they were yet looking on\nفَمَا اسْتَطَاعُوْا مِنْ قِيَامٍ وَّمَا كَانُوْا مُنْتَصِرِيْنَۙ‏(45)\nFAMAA TATAA-O’O MIN QEEAMIN WA MAA KAANOO MUNTASEREENA.\nThen they could not even rise (on their feet), nor could they help themselves\nوَقَوْمَ نُوْحٍ مِّنْ قَبْلُ‌ؕ اِنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا قَوْمًا فٰسِقِيْنَ‏(46)\nWA QAWMA NOOHIN MIN QABL WA INNAHUM KAANOO QAWMAN FAASEQEEN.\nAnd the people of Noah before (that)’, Verily they were wicked people\nوَ السَّمَآءَ بَنَيْنٰهَا بِاَيْٮدٍ وَّاِنَّا لَمُوْسِعُوْنَ‏(47)\nWA SAMAAA-AD BANAYNAAHAA BEAAYDIN WWAANNAA LAMOOSEU’OONA.\nAnd the heaven, We did raise it up with (Our) Might, and verily We are the expanders (of it) expanse?\nوَالْاَرْضَ فَرَشْنٰهَا فَنِعْمَ الْمٰهِدُوْنَ‏(48)\nWAL ARZA FARASHNAAHAA FA NE’MA AL-MAAHEDOONA.\nAnd the earth, We did spread it out (like a carpet), how Excellent (are We) the Spreaders (thereof)?\nوَمِنْ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ خَلَقْنَا زَوْجَيْنِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(49)\nWA MIN KULLE SHAY-IN KHALAQNAL ZAWJAYNE LA-A’LLAKUM TAZAKKAROON.\nAnd of everything have We created in pairs, that ye may reflect?\nفَفِرُّوْۤا اِلَى اللّٰهِ‌ؕ اِنِّىْ لَكُمْ مِّنْهُ نَذِيْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‌ۚ‏(50)\nFAFERROOA ELAL LAAH INNEE LAKUM MINHO NAZEERUM MOBEEN.\nSo fly ye unto God! Verily I am unto you a plain Warner\nوَلَا تَجْعَلُوْا مَعَ اللّٰهِ اِلٰهًا اٰخَرَ‌ؕ اِنِّىْ لَكُمْ مِّنْهُ نَذِيْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‌ۚ‏(51)\nWA LAA TAJ-A’LOO LAAHA LAAHE ELAAHANW AAAKHARA INNEE LAKUM MINHO NAZEERUM MOBEEN.\nSet ye not with God any other god; Verily I am unto you a plain Warner\nكَذٰلِكَ مَاۤ اَتَى الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ مِّنْ رَّسُوْلٍ اِلَّا قَالُوْا سَاحِرٌ اَوْ مَجْنُوْنٌ‌ۚ‏(52)\nKAZAALEKA MAA AATAA LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM MIN RASOOLIN ILLAA QAALOO SAAHERUN AW MAJNOONUN.\nEven so there came not unto those before them an apostle but said they (of him): ‘A sorcerer or a mad man\nاَتَوَاصَوْا بِهٖ‌ۚ بَلْ هُمْ قَوْمٌ طَاغُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(53)\nAATAWAASAWA BEHI BAL HUM QAWMUN TAAGHOONA.\nHave they charged this unto one another? Nay! they are rebellious people\nفَتَوَلَّ عَنْهُمْ فَمَاۤ اَنْتَ بِمَلُوْمٍ‏(54)\nFA TAWALLA A’NHUM FAMAA ANTA BEMALOOMIN.\nThen turn thou thy back upon them for thou art not to be blamed\nوَّذَكِّرْ فَاِنَّ الذِّكْرٰى تَنْفَعُ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(55)\nWWAZAKKER FA-INNAL ZIKRAA TANFAU’U MOAMENEEN.\nAnd remind thou, for verily reminding profiteth the believers\nوَمَا خَلَقْتُ الْجِنَّ وَالْاِنْسَ اِلَّا لِيَعْبُدُوْنِ‏(56)\nWA MAA KHALAQTU AL-JENNA WAL AENSA ILLAA LEEA’BUDOONE.\nAnd created not I, the Jinn and the humans, but that they may worship (Me)\nمَاۤ اُرِيْدُ مِنْهُمْ مِّنْ رِّزْقٍ وَّمَاۤ اُرِيْدُ اَنْ يُّطْعِمُوْنِ‏(57)\nMAA OREEDO MINHUM MIN RREZQIN WA MAA OREEDO AN YYUTE’EMOONE.\nI desire not from them any sustenance, nor do I desire that they should feed Me\nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ هُوَ الرَّزَّاقُ ذُو الْقُوَّةِ الْمَتِيْنُ‏(58)\nINNAL LAAHA HOWA AR-RAZZAAQU ZUL QUWWAH AL-MATEENU.\nVerily, God He (alone) is the Bestower of sustenance, the Lord of the unbreakable strength\nفَاِنَّ لِلَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا ذَنُوْبًا مِّثْلَ ذَنُوْبِ اَصْحٰبِهِمْ فَلَا يَسْتَعْجِلُوْنِ‏(59)\nFA-INNAL LILLAZEENA ZALAMOO ZANOOBAN MISLA ZANOOBE AASHAABEHEM FALAA YASTAA’JELOONE.\nSo, verily those who are unjust shall have a share (of the burden) like unto the share (of the burden) which had their fellows (of old), Therefore, let them ask Me not to hasten it on\nفَوَيْلٌ لِّلَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا مِنْ يَّوْمِهِمُ الَّذِىْ يُوْعَدُوْنَ‏(60)\nLAHUM LIL-LAZEENA KAFAROO MIN YYAWMEHEMU LAZEE YOOA’ADOONA.\nTherefore, Woe unto those who disbelieve because of their day which they are promised!",
  "merits": "Surah al-Zaareyaat (The Scatterers)\nThere are 60 verses in this Surah and it was revealed in Makkah. In the commentary of Majma’ul Bayan it is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that the reward for reciting this Surah is ten times the number of moving winds or breezes.\nImam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that recitation of this Surah increases ones sustenance and makes it easy to earn. Drinking water in which this Surah was dissolved after being written acts as a remedy for back problems (e.g. backaches). If a pregnant woman wears a talisman of Surah al-Zaareyaat, her pregnancy and delivery will be easy. Keeping this Surah close to a dying person makes his death easy."
}
